# Boss_BeamShip_BoltFrameByHeading: the fifth case (ruling 5, 2), at its first call: the bolt's
# heading $2A(a6) at or below $1F4 (more than 3 steps of $8 off due left, $200), so a4 steps past
# all four tests to the last case word. The heading is the bolt's flight angle (10-bit, masked
# with $3FE); the corpus's bolts all flew within $1F6-$20E+ of due left (cases 1-4), the fifth
# case is the same tilt one step further (the bolt's sprite for it is in the script's case table,
# inferred: an aim at a player further off the ship's line than any corpus run stood).

case heading_1F0
w a6 + $2A = $01F0

case heading_100
w a6 + $2A = $0100
